  "preamble": "Spirantization turns the voiceless bilabial stop [p] into the voiceless velar fricative [x]: the stop closure is released into frication and the labial place of articulation is replaced by a dorsal one. Udege and Oroch (Southern Tungusic) changed initial Proto-Tungusic *p to x (*palgan 'foot' > xaga, *pokta 'road' > xokto), while their close relative Nanai keeps p. The change is confined to one branch of a single family, so it is rare.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Lenition, Spirantization",
  "languageExamples": [
    {
      "language": "Proto-Tungusic to Udege and Oroch",
      "languageFamily": "Southern Tungusic",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "*palgan 'foot'",
          "to": "Udege, Oroch хага (xaga)",
          "note": "Nanai палган keeps p; Udege has distinct /x/ and /h/ phonemes."
        },
        {
          "from": "*pokta 'road'",
          "to": "Udege, Oroch хокто (xokto)",
          "note": "Nanai and Orok покто keep p."
        },
        {
          "from": "*palŋa 'palm of hand'",
          "to": "Udege хан’а (xańa), Oroch хаӈа (xaŋa)",
          "note": "Nanai пайӈа (pajŋa) keeps p."
        },
        {
          "from": "*pökti- 'to run'",
          "to": "Udege, Oroch хукти- (xukti-)",
          "note": "Nanai пукчӣни keeps p."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "Sakhalin Ainu",
